dergoing cancer treatment, leading to difficulties in maintaining proper nutrition and hydration.", "HIPODERMOCLISIS:A method of subcutaneous rehydration that is preferred when oral intake is restricted, requiring changes every 4-5 days due to absorption issues.", "ALPERS DH:Author of a study on nutritional considerations in wasting diseases, contributing to the field of nutritional therapeutics.", "ASPEN BOARD OF DIRECTORS:The ASPEN Board of Directors is a governing body responsible for establishing and overseeing guidelines and standards related to parenteral and enteral nutrition practices in medical settings. This board plays a crucial role in ensuring that nutrition support therapy is effectively implemented for both adult and pediatric patients. The ASPEN Board of Directors is dedicated to providing comprehensive guidelines that facilitate the appropriate use of nutrition practices, thereby enhancing patient care and outcomes in various clinical environments.", "BARRERA R:Author of a study on nutritional support in cancer patients, contributing to the field of nutritional therapeutics.", "DE BLAUW I:Author of a study on metabolic changes in cancer anorexia, contributing to the field of nutritional therapeutics.", "GISBERT AGUILAR A:Author of a study on asthenia, cachexia, anorexia, and dehydration, contributing to the field of nutritional therapeutics.", "PLANAS DOMINGO J:Author of a study on cachexia-anorexia, contributing to the field of nutritional therapeutics.", "SANMARTÍN MOREIRA:Sanmartín Moreira is the editor of clinical guidelines on palliative care published in Madrid by Aran in 2007.", "PLANAS DOMINGO:Planas Domingo is an author who contributed to the clinical guidelines on caquexia-anorexia published in Madrid by Aran in 2008.", "RICO PAZOS:Rico Pazos is an author who wrote about nutrition and hydration for terminal patients in a publication edited by Gómez Sancho in Las Palmas de Gran Canaria in 2003.", "SCHATTNER:Schattner is an author who discussed enteral nutritional support for cancer patients in a clinical gastroenterology journal in 2003.", "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARI LA FE:Hospital Universitari La Fe is a hospital located in Valencia, Spain, involved in pediatric artificial nutrition.", "GÓMEZ SANCHO:Gómez Sancho is the editor of a publication on advances in palliative care, which includes contributions on nutrition for terminal patients."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}